# Staged 2026-11-24 from fisher-8ie rules 1 and 9 as amended by D25.
# The held move is sent before exit. The original search sources follow.
# Four-ply info spelling from Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), read 2026-11-24:
# UCIEngine::on_update_full in src/uci.cpp and SearchManager::output_pv in src/search.cpp.
# fisher-r6y D41 sets this spelling; fisher-8hc.6 committed these sessions.
# D3-D6 supply the
# existing principal variation and allowances, with time at least one under D41.
# The fisher-2aj.2 sources below supply the retained scores, node counts and response order.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7, 9 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Starting score: four-ply minimax with python-chess 1.11.2 followed rules
# 1 to 7. An independent reviewer reproduced cp 0 and per-ply counts
# 20/400/8902/197281 with their own minimax. See expectations/perft.epd.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
> position startpos
> go infinite
# Read the search info before sending isready. The move is held.
# D25 releases it on quit or the end of input as well as on stop.
# Rules 1 to 7 and 10. Published perft counts sum to 206603. See the header for cp 0.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 206603 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
# UCI go infinite and isready. No bestmove precedes readyok.
< readyok
! eof
< bestmove {legal}
! exit
